<title>USA: NE Utils says 13,900 still without power.</title>
<headline>NE Utils says 13,900 still without power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northeast Utilities said about 13,900 of its 1.9 million electricity customers were still without service early Wednesday following Sunday's storm storm, which knocked trees onto power lines and transformers.</p>
<p>About 2,500 customers in Connecticut were still lacking power, a steep drop from Monday's tally of 100,000.</p>
<p>In western Massachusetts, there were still 400 power outages, while about 11,000 customers were without power in New Hampshire, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Power is expected to be restored to all Connecticut customers by midnight Wednesday, he said.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
</text>
